{"name":"Salt","hex":"#efede6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Salt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in Salt and Enson parish, Stafford borough, Staffordshire, England .","A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Salt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salt","blocks":[{"text":"Salt is a mineral composed primarily of sodium chloride (NaCl). When used in food, especially in granulated form, it is more formally called table salt. In the form of a natural crystalline mineral, salt is also known as rock salt or halite. Salt is essential for life in general, and saltiness is one of the basic human tastes. Salt is one of the oldest and most ubiquitous food seasonings, and is known to uniformly improve the taste perception of food. Salting, brining, and pickling are ancient and important methods of food preservation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg/330px-Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt","wikidata":"Q11254"},{"title":"Salt (chemistry)","blocks":[{"text":"In chemistry, a salt or ionic compound is a chemical compound consisting of an assembly of positively charged ions (cations) and negatively charged ions (anions), which results in a compound with no net electric charge. The constituent ions are held together by electrostatic forces termed ionic bonds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/NaCl_bonds.svg/330px-NaCl_bonds.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_(chemistry)","wikidata":"Q12370"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Salzproduktion-Halle.jpg/500px-Salzproduktion-Halle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Salzproduktion-Halle.jpg/500px-Salzproduktion-Halle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salt production in Halle, Saxony-Anhalt, 1670","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalzproduktion-Halle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg/500px-Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg/1280px-Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg/500px-Salinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ponds near Maras, Peru, fed from a mineral spring and used for salt production since pre-Inca times ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalinas_de_Maras%2C_Peru-20Sept2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Single_grain_of_table_salt_%28electron_micrograph%29.jpg/500px-Single_grain_of_table_salt_%28electron_micrograph%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Single_grain_of_table_salt_%28electron_micrograph%29.jpg/500px-Single_grain_of_table_salt_%28electron_micrograph%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A SEM image of a grain of table salt","link":"https://en.wikipe